  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-02-24T22:34:22.679Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Absolutely disappointed by the swing-and-miss implementation of OSC when initially advertised to provide native face/eye-tracking integration. As-is, the current implementation functions no better than prohibited third-party tools, aside from not having to load those libraries. No avatar currently has enough parameter memory to allow for all of the face tracking blend shapes, and it gets too close for comfort if you're trying to get creative with combined animation trees.\nAny plans for giving the API access to the paths for avatar blendshapes/transforms? Without this, you guys are going to continue to fall behind the curve compared to other platforms for compatibility. Documentation states API only has access to the avatar parameters list and control inputs.\n\nEdit: If the concern is that no two tracker APIs are the same (IE: Vive vs Pimax eye trackers), just leave that up to the 3rd-party app we have to sideload to figure out. Seems you've already decided to (somewhat ironically) go the route of relying on 3rd-party software despite using this as a method to get rid of some. Embrace it at this point - but we still need access to these data points to do it right.",
